From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jun Matsushita <jun@mercury.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:55:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] examples/bes: check what buck2 sends a Build Event
 Service, in CI

`examples/bes/check.py` runs buck2 against `fake_bes_server.py`, a Build
Event Service that records every event it receives. It checks four commands:

- A build that succeeds streams a complete invocation, from `started` to
  `build_finished` and the end of the stream.
- A build that fails reports its exit code in `build_finished`.
- A test run reports the status of each test.
- `buck2 kill --bes-drain-timeout` delivers a stream that the daemon still
  held when its command ended. The server for this case reads slowly and
  acknowledges only at the end of a stream, as BuildBuddy does. Without the
  drain, the kill loses the last events of the stream, `build_finished`
  among them.

The Linux job of the Build and Examples workflow runs it on the release
binary, beside the NativeLink example. It needs no secret and no outside
service. The Python stubs come from the protos under `remote_execution/oss`,
generated with a pinned `grpcio-tools`.

The e2e tests under `tests/` would be the usual home, but open source does
not run them, and builds with `fbcode_build` set compile the BES sink out.

